  [ceiling · answered] Functional upper end walls of the four rotated WAGO wells. Each flat 9.4 × 8.7 mm underside closes the rectangular pocket at one end of its 19.1 mm vertical body allowance, with 3 mm stock above it. The rear half of the connector slides into this rectangular seat along its own Y axis; its levers and the west face remain accessible. Tree(auto)/Default retains its automatic supports, which are removed through the open well mouth. The current native slice records their placement; physical release remains unmeasured.
    alternatives: Filling the pocket below this end wall occupies the WAGO body. Sloping the underside enters that rectangular body allowance; retaining it with a thicker rising section raises the upper row toward the funnel frame. Opening the end removes axial capture of the connector. The current end wall preserves its purchased rectangular mating envelope.
